-- title:
--   Frobenius acts by ± q on a line in the eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer and $g$ a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients at all primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$), such that $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ is the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero that is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $K$. On $J_0(M)=\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the level-$M$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ take the Hecke-module structure `heckeModuleBar`, and let $T=$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) be the module of sequences $x:\mathbb{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$. Assume given: a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ acting in level $n$ through reduction $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda\to\mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$; a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ with $\rho_M(\sigma)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes y$ whenever $y=\sigma\cdot x$ componentwise; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell \text{ prime}]$ to the same endomorphism ring with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of $K$-dimension $2$, stable under every base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(X_\ell)$ acts by the scalar $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$. Then for every prime $q\neq\lambda$ with $q\mid M$ and $q^2\nmid M$, and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, there are a $K$-submodule $L\le W$ of dimension $1$ and an element $a\in K$ with $a^2=1$ such that for every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $A$ for $q$ — that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^q$ — the base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$ acts on $L$ by the scalar $a\cdot q$, and $\rho_M(\sigma)w-a\cdot w\in L$ for all $w\in W$.
--
--   This records the local shape at a prime exactly dividing the level of the $\lambda$-adic representation cut out by a weight-two newform: on a decomposition group at $q\,\|\,M$ the two-dimensional eigenplane is an extension of an unramified quadratic character $\chi$ by its cyclotomic twist $\chi\varepsilon$, the invariant line being the one on which Frobenius acts by $\chi(\mathrm{Frob}_q)q=\pm q$. It is used by [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_torLine_of_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_eq_qCoeff`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_torLine_of_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_eq_qCoeff), which identifies the scalar $a$ with the $q$-th coefficient of $g$.
